rx550-g5-kde: KDE Plasma fixes for big-endian Power Mac G5 (optional)
======================================================================

KDE Plasma 6.7.5 on a big-endian G5 needs fixes in three places. Two are in the rx550-g5 kernel
and Mesa packages; this optional package carries the one that lives in KDE itself:

* plasma-workspace (Plasma X11 only): OutputOrderWatcher reads the 32-bit X11 _KDE_SCREEN_INDEX
  property as a single byte. On big-endian that byte is 0, Plasma thinks every screen is disabled
  and plasmashell shows a black desktop with only a mouse pointer.

This package does not replace plasma-workspace. A pacman hook (96-rx550-g5-kde.hook) runs
/usr/lib/rx550-g5/kde-be-fix after every plasma-workspace install or upgrade; it finds the one
"load byte" instruction behind the bug in libkworkspace6.so by pattern and turns it into "load word"
(4 bytes changed). If the pattern is not found exactly once (for example after KDE fixes the bug)
nothing is changed. Removing the package reverts the change. pacman -Qkk plasma-workspace reports
libkworkspace6.so as modified while the fix is in place; that is expected.

  /usr/lib/rx550-g5/kde-be-fix --check     show the state
  /usr/lib/rx550-g5/kde-be-fix --revert    undo by hand

Not needed for Plasma (Wayland), the default session: there plasmashell gets the screen order over
Wayland. Wayland on the G5 needs the rx550-g5 kernel (ADDFB2 on big-endian) and Mesa (EGL/Wayland
formats), which the main packages provide.

Source patches for KDE (plasma-workspace, and a KWin fallback that is not reached with the
rx550-g5 kernel): https://github.com/parabellum-push/rx550-g5/tree/main/packaging/arch/kde
